{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Cursed are you from among all the cattle and from among all the beasts of the field.</b> Following what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Ta'anit 8a): In the future all the beasts will gather beside the serpent and say, 'The lion tears prey and eats, etc. — what benefit do you have?' and so forth — therefore it is said that it will be cursed more than every beast of the field, for they all have some aspect of benefit from what they tear and devour, whereas the serpent has no benefit whatsoever, for there is no advantage for the owner of the tongue; therefore it will have no pleasure in its trampling, as stated. And if you were to say that the מֵם of 'מִכָּל' is not a מֵם of excess [i.e., 'more than'], then explain it thus: that it will be cursed from the mouth of them all, for all the beasts will gather to you and curse you and despise you, and before your face they will answer your wickedness, saying, 'What benefit do you have?'"], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:26:52.217365043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}